# Stray signal files from the `claude-notify-extension` Stop/Notification/
# PermissionRequest hooks in ~/.claude/settings.json. Their commands are
# `touch C:\Users\Madhav\.claude\claude-notify-signals\<signal>`, but Claude
# Code runs hooks through Git Bash, where `\U`, `\M`, `\c` etc. are escapes:
# the backslashes are eaten, the path collapses to one relative filename, and
# `touch` creates it in whatever directory the session is running in.
#
# Matched on the distinctive middle of the name rather than its `C:` prefix:
# NTFS cannot hold a colon, so the character on disk is U+F03A, which git sees
# as three bytes while msys bash renders it back as `:`. A `C:*` pattern
# therefore never matches, and `git check-ignore` reads it as an absolute path.
*claude-notify-signals*
.cairn/queue/
.cairn/traces/
.cairn/review-log.jsonl
